[ti:Week03-Thur.mp3]

[00:00.00]triple 熟义 a. 三人的，三部分的，三组的；三倍的，三重的‖v. 成为三倍，使增至三倍 示例 ① Things can get a bit dicey when we begin to speak of "national character," but in Japan's response to 2011's triple disaster of earthquake, tsunami, and nuclear meltdown, the world saw a people react to biblical hardship with inspiring decency, dignity, and resolve. 当我们讨论国民性格的时候多少会有些不确定，但是日本国民在应对2011年地震、海啸、核泄漏这三起灾难的时候，让世人看到了这个民族在对抗圣经中描述过的苦难时所表现出的令人鼓舞的体面、尊严和决心。（The Daily Beast）② Output should triple next month. 到下月产量应增至三倍。
[00:11.57]generate 熟义 v. 产生，引起 示例 ① If these investments generate huge social benefits—as they clearly do— the benefits of providing more social support for the family should be that much clearer. 如果这些投资能够带来巨大的社会效益——事实显然如此——那么为家庭提供更多社会支持的好处应该会更加明显。（2010. 6）② We need somebody to generate new ideas. 我们需要有人想出新主意。
[00:18.76]surpass 熟义 v. 超过，胜过，优于 示例 ① No physicist is likely to surpass Einstein in the next 200 years. 在之后的两百年间，没有物理学家能够超过爱因斯坦。（2010. 12）② His success has surpassed all expectations. 他所取得的成功远远超出了预期。
[00:23.25]participant 熟义 n. 参与者，参加者 示例 ① Each week, one of the participants would be eliminated from the show, with the winner receiving a trip to the Mir space station. 每周，将有一名参赛者被淘汰，最终胜出者的奖品是一趟和平号空间站之旅。（2006. 12） ② He has been an active participant in the sports meeting. 他一直积极参加运动会。
[00:29.67]alarm 熟义 n. 警报；警报器；惊慌，恐慌‖v. 使惊慌，使害怕；给门等安装警报器 示例 ① For the next ten years a succession of books, mainly by Americans, sounded the alarm. 在接下来的十年里，主要由美国人撰写的一系列图书 （给全世界）敲响了警钟。（2010. 12） ② I decided to sound the alarm. 我决定发出警报。
[00:34.93]strive 熟义 v. 努力，奋斗，力求，力争 示例 ① Young Indians strive for fluency in English. 印度年轻一代为讲一口流利的英语而努力。（The Guardian） ② They encourage all members to strive for the highest standards. 他们鼓励所有成员为最高标准而奋斗。
[00:39.50]arson 熟义 n. 放火（罪），纵火（罪） 示例 ① The violence is steadily escalating: smashed windows and looted stores have led to the arson of vehicles and buildings and mass confrontations with riot police. 暴力事件正在逐步升级：砸坏的玻璃和洗劫的商店激发了对车辆和建筑物的纵火行为并导致了与防暴警察的大规模对抗。（www.foreignpolicy.com）② They want to carry out an arson attack. 他们想进行纵火袭击。
[00:47.16]stabilise 熟义 v.（使）稳固，稳定 示例 ① The next three weeks are absolutely critical, and they can still stabilise the markets. 接下来的三个星期是绝对重要的，他们仍然能使市场稳定。（The New York Times）② The doctors stabilised his condition. 那些医生使他的病情稳定了下来。
[00:52.40]expenditure 熟义 n. 花费，消费，费用，开支；（精力、 时间等的）耗费，消耗 示例 ① The change cut their expenditures in half, but the new living arrangement proved too challenging. 这种改变节省了他们一半的开销，但是结果证明新的居住安排太有挑战性了。（2012. 12） ② This study represents an expenditure of effort. 这项研究意味着要耗费大量的精力。
[00:58.68]principle 熟义 n. 道德原则；原理；信条；定律 示例 ① "The key principle of copyright law has always been that works can be copied only once authors have expressly given their permission," says Piers Blofeld, of the Sheil Land literary agency in London. 伦敦希尔•兰德作家代理公司的皮尔斯•布洛菲尔德说：“著作权法最主要的原则始终是：著作只有在得到作者明确表示允许的情况下才可以复制”。（2011. 12） ② Stick to your principles and tell her you won't do it. 要恪守自己的原则，告诉她你决不会那么做。
[01:07.93]era 熟义 n. 时代，纪元，年代；地质年代 示例 ① America's most popular newspaper website today announced that the era of free online journalism is drawing to a close. 美国最受欢迎的报纸网站今天宣布，免费在线新闻时代已经接近尾声。（2010. 12） ② When he left the firm, it was an end of an era. 他离开公司后，一个时代结束了。
[01:13.86]assess 熟义 v. 评估，评定；估算，核定 示例 ① Each group consisted of around 120 adults of similar age and education, and the test assessed their language skills. 每个小组由大约120名年龄相仿、教育背景相似的成年人组成，测试评估了他们的语言水平。（2010. 6） ② It is hard to assess the effects of these changes. 这些变化带来的效果难以评估。
[01:20.14]impose 熟义 v. 迫使，把…强加于 示例 ① The very ambition we impose on our children may get some into Harvard but may also set them up for disappointment. 正是我们强加在孩子身上的那种野心可能使一些孩子进入哈佛大学，但是也可能给他们带来失望。（2008. 6） ② He didn't want to impose his values on his friends. 他不想勉强朋友接受自己的价值观。
[01:26.34]insight 熟义 n. 洞察力，领悟；洞悉，了解 示例 ① The independence created by philosophical insight is—in my opinion— the mark of distinction between a mere artisan or specialist and a real seeker after truth. 我认为哲学思维所培养的独立是区分工匠或行家与真正的真理探索者的标志。（2010. 12） ② He is a writer with great insight. 他是一位有深刻洞察力的作家。
[01:33.14]manifest 熟义 v. 表明，清楚显示；使人注意到 示例 ① She said he didn't seem to manifest other symptoms of psychotic behaviour—he dressed well, paid his bills —and, besides his claims of surveillance, which sounded paranoid, he behaved normally. 她说他看上去没有其他精神病行为的明显症状——他衣着得体，支付账单，除了有自称受到监视的类似幻想外，他一切正常。（The Washington Post）② The anger he felt is manifest in his works. 他感受到的愤怒明显地表现在他的作品中。
[01:41.98]presumably 熟义 ad. 很可能，大概，想必是 示例 ① Some people were more likely to eat fatty foods, presumably because they thought being fat was their genetic destiny and saw no sense in fighting it. 一些人会更倾向于摄入高脂肪食物，这很可能是因为他们认为肥胖是由自身基因导致的， 并且觉得对抗肥胖毫无意义。（The New York Times） ② He will be taking the car, presumably? 想必他是要买这辆汽车了？
[01:49.31]prime 熟义 a. 主要的，首要的；基本的‖n. 盛年， 鼎盛时期 示例 ① A formidable wall of bureaucracy has been erected to protect their prime nesting sites on the Atlantic coastlines. 为了保护它们（海龟）在大西洋沿岸的主要筑巢地，官方机构已建立起了一堵坚固的墙。（2009. 6） ② His prime concern is how to protect his property. 他最关心的是如何保护自己的财产。
[01:55.78]whereas 熟义 conj. 然而；鉴于 示例 ① At the Polytechnic I'd have to do 35 hours a week, 20 teaching and 15 administration, whereas the Pistoia School is only asking for 30 hours' teaching. 在理工学院我每周要工作35个小时，其中20个小时教课、15个小时管理，然而皮斯托亚学校只要求教课30个小时。（2010. 6） ② Some of the studies show satisfactory results, whereas others do not.有一些研究结果令人满意，然而其他的则不然。
[02:03.77]band 熟义 n. 乐队；带；一帮人‖v. 加彩条；划分档次 示例 ① In college there was no time for bands, but I joined the University of Houston Chorus, and traveled to performances around the state with that august group. 上大学时没有时间参加乐队， 但是我加入了休斯顿大学的合唱队，并且和这个尊贵的团体一起巡游全国演出。（Psychology Today）② She persuaded a small band of volunteers to help.她劝服了一小批志愿者来帮忙。
[02:11.51]consolidate 熟义 vt. 使加强，使巩固‖vi. 结成一体，合并 示例 ① A failure to consolidate and widen their cooperation would damage not just both nations but the world as a whole. 如果两国合作关系不能得到巩固和拓展，受到损害的不仅是这两个国家，还有整个世界。（The New York Times）② The two firms consolidated for greater efficiency. 为提高效率，这两家公司合并了。
[02:18.32]slap 熟义 vt.（用手掌）拍，打，掴‖n. （用手掌）拍，打，捆 示例 ① There was a look of consternation on her face; she looked like she wanted to slap me but couldn't bring herself to do it. 她脸上带着惊慌失措的表情，看上去想要打我一巴掌，可又下不去手。（The New Yorker）② She slapped him hard across the face. 她狠狠地给了他一巴掌。
[02:24.41]amount 熟义 n. 金额；数量‖v. 总计；相当于 示例 ① I have never had to justify the amount I am spending to the company's founders. 我向来用不着向公司创始人说明我的开销用之有道。（2011. 12）② His answer amounted to a complete refusal. 他的答复相当于完全拒绝。
[02:29.17]consume 熟义 v. 消耗；吃，喝；使充满（强烈的感情）；毁灭 示例 ① Forty percent of that powers old-fashioned incandescent light bulbs—a 19th-century technology that wastes most of the power it consumes on unwanted heat. 这其中的40%用于为老式的白炽灯泡供电——19世纪一项将大部分的电能用于产生不需要的热能的技术。（2007. 12） ② The restaurant was quickly consumed by fire. 那家餐厅很快被大火吞噬了。
[02:36.75]integrate 熟义 v.（使）合并，成为一体；（使）加入，融入群体 示例 ① Perhaps most significant, according to Mannaz, is the increasing interest large companies have in more collaborative management models, such as those prevalent in Scandinavia, which seek to integrate the hard and soft aspects of leadership and encourage delegated responsibility and accountability. 根据马南兹的研究，或许最值得注意的是大型公司越来越对协作式的管理模式感兴趣，正如在斯堪的纳维亚半岛流行的那种管理模式一样，它力图整合领导方式中强硬和温和的方面，鼓励落实责任和义务。（2011. 6）② She has not made any effort to integrate with the local community. 她完全没有尝试融入当地社区。
[02:49.50]candidate 熟义 n. 候选人，申请人；应试者 示例 ① Professor Gauthier believes schools should not just be selecting candidates from traditional sectors such as banking, consultancy and industry. 高蒂尔教授认为，学校不应该只从传统行业如银行业、咨询业和工业领域选取候选人。（2011. 6）② There are a large number of candidates for the job. 有许多求职者应聘这份工作。
[02:56.50]horizon 熟义 n. 地平线；范围；眼界 示例 ① Therefore we try, through our policies, performance, and communications, to attract new shareholders who understand our operations, share our time horizons, and measure us as we measure ourselves. 因此我们试着通过我们的政策、表现与沟通， 吸引理解我们的经营模式、认可我们的投资回报期并用我们评估自己的方式来评估我们的新股东。（The Economist）② He wanted to travel to broaden his horizons. 他想通过旅行来开阔眼界。
[03:05.29]assert 熟义 v. 断言；主张 示例 ① Many Syrians in the capital had long asserted that the uprising-turned-civil war would not breach the city centre. 许多在首都的叙利亚人一直宣称：由起义演变而成的人民战争不会破坏城市中心。（The Guardian）② He continued to assert that he was innocent. 他仍然坚称自己是无辜的。
[03:11.18]contact 熟义 n. 联系；接触；交往‖v. 联系，联络 示例 ① Both strains quickly invaded local hospitals where needle sharing and other unhealthy practices ensured the rapid spreading of the infection by bringing people into contact with contaminated body fluids. 当地医院里的针头多人共用以及其他一些不卫生的操作使人们接触到受污染的体液，为感染的迅速传播提供了条件，两种菌株（因此）迅速侵入了当地的医院。（2013. 6）② I don't have much contact with my aunt. 我和姑姑很少联系。
[03:20.14]command 熟义 n. 命令，指令；指挥‖v. 命令；控制； 值得 示例 ① Anything in your home that uses electricity can be put on the home network and at your command. 你家里任何需要用电的装置都可以接入到家庭网络并由你控制。（www.howstaffworks.com）② The army is now under the direct command of General Barton. 这支军队现在由巴顿将军直接指挥。
[03:26.42]conceal 熟义 v. 隐藏，隐瞒 示例 ① Known as cephalopods, these animals have the extraordinary ability to conceal themselves from predators by adjusting their skin to take on the colors, shapes and patterns of their local environment. 这些头足类动物在隐藏自己、 躲避捕食者方面可谓身手不凡——调节肤色、改变体形与身体的花纹，从而达到与周边环境一致。（www.foxnews.com） ② Tom could barely conceal his disappointment. 汤姆几乎掩饰不住自己的失望。
[03:35.09]delicate 熟义 a. 易碎的；纤弱的；精美的；精致的 示例 ① For example, doctors did not have devices allowing them to go inside the human body to detect health problems or to perform delicate surgery. 例如，医生没有可以进入人体探测人们健康状况或者实施精密手术的设备。（2011. 12） ② Eyes are one of the most delicate organs of the body. 眼睛是人体最娇贵的器官之一。
[03:41.93]overwhelm 熟义 v. 充溢；征服；压垮 示例 ① This trend results in emergency rooms being overwhelmed with patients without regular doctors. 这种趋势导致的结果是：急救室里挤满了没有日常初级护理医生护理的病人。（2009. 12） ② He was overwhelmed by feelings of guilt. 他感到愧疚难当。
[03:47.21]efficiency 熟义 n. 效率；功效，效能 示例 ① Efficiency is also a great way to lower carbon emissions and help slow global warming. 能效也是降低碳排放量和减缓全球变暖的有效方法。（2007. 12） ② I was impressed by the efficiency with which he handled the crisis. 他应对危机效率之高给我留下了深刻的印象。
[03:52.89]sample 熟义 n. 样品，样本‖v. 取样；尝试，体验 示例 ① Within samples collected from the solid substance lying beneath the ice, they found fossils of microscopic marine plants which suggest that the region was once an open ocean—not solid ice. 他们在冰层下搜集的固体样本中发现了海洋微生物的化石，这说明这一地区曾经是开放的海洋而不是固态冰。（2010. 12） ② The investigation covers a representative sample of schools. 调查覆盖了一些有代表性的学校。
[04:01.54]originate 熟义 v. 起源，发源；创建，发明 示例 ① But not all investigators agree that dream imagery originates in visual areas. Several dream researchers have proposed the opposite path, suggesting that dreams originate in the regions that store memories and then connect to visual brain areas. 但并非所有调查者都同意睡梦中的情景源于大脑的视觉区，有好几个梦境研究者提出了相反的看法：梦境源于储存记忆并把它与大脑视觉区连接起来的区域。（Scientific American）② The disease is said to have originated in the tropics. 据说，这种疾病起源于热带地区。
[04:12.17]core 熟义 n. 果心；地核；要点‖a. 核心的 示例 ① Google's core business is search and find, so obviously what helps improve Google's search engine is good for Google. 谷歌的核心业务是搜索和发现，因此显而易见，能帮助谷歌改进搜索引擎的就对谷歌有利。（2011. 12） ② Concern for the environment is at the core of their policies. 对环境的关注是他们政策的核心。
[04:18.78]option 熟义 n. 选择；选修课；选项 示例 ① Judson College, a 350-student institution in Alabama, has offered students a three-year option for 40 years. 杰德森学院是阿拉巴马州一所拥有350名学生的学校，40年来它一直为学生提供三年制学位。（2012. 6）② There are various options open to him. 他有多种选择。
[04:24.46]flaw 熟义 n. 缺点；裂痕；弱点 示例 ① By the end of the summer, he realised the mathematical approach he had been pursuing for almost three years was flawed. 到那年夏末，他意识到他一直使用了近三年的数学方法有缺陷。（2007. 12） ② There is always a flaw in the personality of a tragic hero. 悲剧主角总有性格上的弱点。
[04:30.44]plug 熟义 n. 插头；插座；塞子‖v. 塞住；供给； 推广 示例 ① We are all used to jumping into our cars, driving 200-300 miles, making a pit stop and then carry on driving. But this mindset is changing as more people swap the pump for the plug when they run out of juice. 我们已经习惯于跳进车里，开上二三百英里，停车加油后继续行驶。但是这种习惯正在改变，更多的人在没油时将油泵换成插头。（CNN） ② The printer is plugged in. 打印机接上电源了。
[04:38.48]superiority 熟义 n. 优势，优越；优越感，优越性 示例 ① Ultimately, our aim should not be to assert the superiority of the physical world over the virtual, but to make them work together. 我们的最终目标不应是证明物质世界相对于虚拟世界的优越性，而是让它们和谐共存。（The Guardian）② She showed an air of superiority. 她摆出一副盛气凌人的架势。
